  "description": [
   {
    "value": "Mark Twain, whose real name was Samuel (Langhorne) Clemens, was born in 1835 in Florida, USA. Before he began writing, Twain worked as a printer, a Mississippi riverboat pilot, a gold prospector, and a reporter. As a writer, he was a major figure in American realism. His two most famous books—\"The Adventures of Tom Sawyer\" (1876) and its sequel, \"The Adventures of Huckleberry Finn\" (1884)—are considered classics of world literature. Twain died in 1910 in Redding, Connecticut.",
    "lang": "en",
    "via": "llm-page:bio under BOOK AUTHOR heading (machine-translated rendering)",
    "file": "P866.json",
    "uri": false
   }
  ],
